   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the assessors of the town of Smithtown and\nthe village of Head of the Harbor, county of Suffolk, to accept from the\nMonastery of the Glorious Ascension Inc., an application for exemption from\nreal property taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S5706",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5706-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5706\n\nSPONSOR: FLANAGAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to authorizing the assessors of the\ntown of Smithtown and the village of Head of the Harbor, county of\nSuffolk, to accept from the Monastery of the Glorious Ascension Inc., an\napplication for exemption from real property taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow the Monastery of the Glorious Ascension, Inc. to apply for a\nretroactive real property tax exemption from the Town of Smithtown and t\nhe Village of Head of the Harbor for 2018 and 2019.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Provides the Monastery of the Glorious Ascension Inc. to\napply for a real property tax exemption from the Town of Smithtown and\nthe Village of Head of the Harbor for the 2018 and 2019 tax years.\n\nSection 2: Sets forth an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOn February 27, 2018 the Monastery of the Glorious Ascension Inc.  d/b/a\nthe Monastery of Saint Dionysios purchased the Timothy House in Saint\nJames, New York to be the new home for the Monastery's nine monks. The\nMonastery has requested retroactive real property tax exemption on the\nnewly acquired property for the 2018 and 2019 assessments in the Town of\nSmithtown and the Village of Head of the Harbor.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: New bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
